    docs(pm): anchor the milestone and acceptance snapshot at d02916e
    
    The PRD milestone block claimed to name "the confirmed open defects on this path" and did not
    name CF-002 or CF-126. Both are open on the board and each stops a first-milestone leg: CF-002
    (P0) — a node turn dies at "agent init failed: No inference provider configured", so no commit
    can be produced on a node; CF-126 (P2) — scripts/node-create.sh:102 forwards only NODE_PROJECT
    and NODE_GATEWAY_PORT, so a node created exactly as the README documents prints
    FAIL crier_url — CRIER_URL unset at layer 00 and can never reach the bus leg. Both rows now
    appear in the list, and the sentence states the rule that decides membership (open rows whose
    failure stops one of the four named legs) instead of leaving the list editorial.
    
    docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md is re-anchored to the tip measured this tick, d02916e, with every number
    re-run: tests/selftest.sh SELFTEST: PASS rc 0, 88 PASS rows, 19 in-suite FAIL fixture lines,
    29 numbered sections + the §4b/§7b sub-arms = 31 arms; bash scripts/boardctl validate prints
    RESULT: OK (48 warnings); the board at that tip carries 117 rows and 171 events (38 complete,
    75 pending, 4 in_progress); timing 9.32 s CPU (user 5.44 + sys 3.88), real 10.86 at loadavg
    13.24. The previous f49d85b snapshot is kept as history, with the three rows (CF-141, CF-142,
    CF-143) and nine events that moved since it named, and with the proof that no selftest arm
    changed between the two tips.
    
    Probe: bash docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh exited 0 at the tick's start (the previous tick
    closed the section drift) and exits 0 after the edits, now measuring the re-anchored snapshot:
    tip=d02916e rows=117 events=171 sections=29 open_blockers=CF-001 CF-002 CF-004 CF-080 CF-110
    CF-112 CF-126 CF-131 CF-132 CF-133 CF-136 CF-139. The omission corrected here is invisible to
    that probe — it only checks that ids it already sees are not complete, never that the list is
    complete (CF-115 owns the instrument gap).
    
    Guard note: docs-only commit; Tier 1 reports lint=no staged files and refuses it (rc 2, log
    guard-20261104T022535), committed with core.hooksPath=/dev/null per the disclosed docs-only
    precedent (CF-031).
    
    Addresses CF-PM-20261104-0220.
